Z||000009||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||11:39 PM||||or remove the clear part of the lights (there are 6 clips all the way aroung the tail light), and cut 1" strips of regular tint and apply to the inside. careful, 1" or less, go higher then 1 and you get wrinkles.<P>This is not my mod, I read it on a Web page.( i forgot where at, to whom thought of it, I appolgize for forgetting)<BR>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker<p>[This message has been edited by SPDFREK (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000010||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||11:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>simply remove your taillight assymblies, remove the colored lens portion, put in colored bulbs, and your done<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>??? is this how people are getting the Clear taillights??? If so, saves me alot of time and money. hehehe<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000011||pontiacs4me||05-31-2001||03:29 AM||||I used nite shades on mine.  I sprayed the outside of the lense, let it dry for about an hour, it had alot of dust in it, and it wasnt as shiny as I hoped, so I sprayed 3 coats of clearcoat on it, then let them dry and sanded and buffed them.  They look awesome.  no orange peel, perfectly smooth and glossy.  When its dark and the lights are on they are a dark cherry red.  Very cool looking.  They shine through probably 85 percent of what they did stock.  I dont have any problems with cops or anything.  A can through summit is 7 bucks, it will do 2 taillights, 2 flushmount parking lights, and all four side markers.   <A HREF="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/fiero10.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/fiero10.jpg</A>  check it out||||reg||1
Z||000012||saleenfiero||05-31-2001||11:02 AM||||Seeing as I can't get to a Summit store and they don't have that stuff in their catalog, I'm screwed for that way, but I might try that tint strip thing as long as it looks good.  I read the article on the top 10 budget enhancments about tinting your lights, but I couldn't figure out one thing, is it 1" wide strips along the length of the light or 1" by 1" pieces?||||reg||1
Z||000013||SPDFREK||05-31-2001||11:33 AM||||HE HE HE, good question! never thought bout it. I would say up down would be the best way to avoid wrinkles, but Summit Racing will send you Free Catalogs.  here is the order page.... <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com/store_bin/freecatalog/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.summitracing.com/store_bin/freecatalog/index.htm</A> <P>Have a question bout the spray stuff though, isn't that the stuff that's supposed to go clear when then lights are turned on? Had a buddy buy some stuff that CLAIMED it would go clear, but it never did hehehe.<P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000014||c m west||05-31-2001||12:17 PM||||the effect that it will give is that it will keep your ass from getting a ticket because you have removed the colored portion of the housing||||reg||1
Z||000015||SPDFREK||05-31-2001||03:04 PM||||What ever Happened to Blue Dots? I have a set in the Nova, but I can't find them anywhere any more. was trying ti see what they would look like on a fiero, o well.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000016||pontiacs4me||05-31-2001||10:16 PM||||It doesnt "go clear"  it lets the light pass through normally.  They appear pitch black until the bulbs are lit, then they shine through (almost) normally.  The color of the taillights when lit are a nice deep cherry red color, I have got a few complements on them.  BTW, the part number for the stuff from summit is VHT-SP999.  and they do list it in the catalog.  In the detailing section.  Call 1800-230-3030.||||reg||1
